{
  "id": "Compound::DB06637 - Gene::3748",
  "verbalization": "Dalfampridine is shown to bind to multiple potassium channel subunits, including Kcna7, Kcnq5, and Kcnh1, all of which are involved in delayed rectifier potassium channel activity. This activity is ultimately linked to the participation of Kcnc3, a key component of the delayed rectifier potassium channel. The high scores in the visible paths suggest a strong, consistent relationship between Dalfampridine and Kcnc3, mediated through the delayed rectifier potassium channel pathway. The mechanism appears to involve Dalfampridine modulating the activity of these channels, which in turn affects Kcnc3. The evidence supports a direct, mechanistic link between Dalfampridine and Kcnc3, with the binding of Dalfampridine to potassium channel subunits playing a central role in this interaction. The pathways are consistent across different subunits, indicating a general effect on the delayed rectifier potassium channel complex.",
